First, find the intercepts. The line $y = x + 4$ intersects $y = 0$ at $(-4,0)$ and the line $x + 3y = 12$. The line $x + 3y = 12$ intersects $y = 0$ at $(12,0)$. The base of the triangle is the distance between the points $(-4,0)$ and $(12,0)$, which is $16$ units. The height is the y-coordinate of the point where $y = x + 4$ intersects $x + 3y = 12$. Solving the system of equations:
\begin{align*}
y &= x + 4 \\
x + 3y &= 12
\end{align*}
Substituting $y = x + 4$ into the second equation gives $x + 3(x + 4) = 12$. Simplifying this gives $4x + 12 = 12$, so $4x = 0$ and $x = 0$. Substituting $x = 0$ into $y = x + 4$ gives $y = 4$. So, the height is $4$ units. The area of the triangle is $\frac{1}{2} \times \text{base} \times \text{height} = \frac{1}{2} \times 16 \times 4 = 32$ square units.</think> <answer>$32$</answer>
